Subject: d3d11: route On12 constant buffers, buffer maps and UpdateSubresource

Almost every real D3D11 frame reads shader constants, and the standalone On12
device rejected all of it: VSSetConstantBuffers and PSSetConstantBuffers (and
their *1 and getter forms) returned after a WARN, UpdateSubresource did the
same, and Map accepted only staging Texture2D readback. A shader with a
cbuffer therefore drew with whatever the driver's slots held.

Route them through the core's new exports (ordinals 47-51):

  - {VS,PS}SetConstantBuffers bind whole buffers through
    WineD3D11On12SetConstantBuffersV1 and retain each bound buffer with
    d3d11_backend_child_bind, as SRVs are retained, so a buffer released
    while bound survives until it is replaced or ClearState runs. The *1
    forms route when they pass no ranges; constant ranges are not routed yet
    and are refused with a WARN rather than bound whole. Getters read the
    retained bindings, and the *1 getters report constant 0 and
    ByteWidth / 16 constants per bound buffer, as D3D11 does.
  - Map/Unmap on an owned buffer go to MapBufferV1/UnmapBufferV1, which pick
    the driver's map family from the buffer's usage and bind flags. Texture2D
    maps are unchanged.
  - UpdateSubresource on an owned buffer or Texture2D goes to UpdateBufferV1
    or UpdateTexture2DV1, which validate the box and pitch before dispatch.
  - ClearState unbinds both stages' constant buffers.

The D3D10 equivalents are not touched: standalone On12 devices are created
d3d11_only, so ID3D10Device is never handed out for them. Other shader stages
keep their rejection; only vertex and pixel shaders exist on this backend.
The new ops are designated members, absent from the WineD3D table, so
ordinary devices keep their WineD3D paths. The five exports resolve as one
required group, so an older core cannot publish a partial backend.

Requires WineD3D11On12{SetConstantBuffers,MapBuffer,UnmapBuffer,UpdateBuffer,
UpdateTexture2D}V1 (ordinals 47-51). Applies after patches 0002-0028 to WineCX
7dbc5b5322a6ef3fb04bdc643c64b188fd641149.

